---
title: Pages
layout: layouts/pagealign.liquid
permalink: /pages/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["page"]
---
{%- comment %} Every page the operator has created, whether or not it is in
   the rail menu (site.json's `navigation` decides that). Pages live at
   /<slug>/, so an index at /pages/ cannot collide with them; a page whose
   slug is "pages" would, and Eleventy refuses that build. Alphabetical by
   title: pages have no date to order by. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign pages = collections.page | sort: "data.title" -%}
{%- if pages.size == 0 -%}
<p>No pages yet. Create one from Indiekit's editor and it appears here.</p>
{%- else -%}
<ul class="collection-list">
{%- for item in pages %}
	<li>
		<a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
		{%- if item.data.summary %}
		<p>{{ item.data.summary }}</p>
		{%- endif %}
	</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endif -%}
